A||||10||FieroFanaticus2||This is bad, really bad!  I need your help ASAP!!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||12-25-2001||12:15 AM||||Ok.  So I lost the keys to my 87 buick lesabre.  My only set.  I've looked everywhere and can't find them.  They are somewhere in the yard.  I think.  I hope.<BR>But my car is parked in somebody elses spot.  I need to find a way to get it started so I can move it, and/or drive it until I find my keys.  I am not stealing somebody elses car.  I have the title, I can show it to you.  Does anybody know an easy (yeah right) way I can get it started and get it moving???  Any help would be appreciated.  Email me if you've got a method.  PLEASE!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||12-25-2001||12:40 AM||||Don't you hate it when that happens? Sorry I can't help you. But I know how you feel! A few weeks ago I got insanely hammered at a party and lost my keys. Worst part is I was driving my fathers car! I looked for them the next day ang found them on the ground next to the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">.<P>Hope it works out for you!<P>Oh, and if worst comes to worse. You can allways try the "jam a flathead screwdriver into slot and turn" meathod. But thats the last thing u want to try,, as you will be replacing the lock cylinder after that.||||reg||11
Z||000002||ejayerik||12-25-2001||12:49 AM||||Try a locksmith. At this time, he will charge you high but aslong as you show him an I.D. and the title that is inside the car, he can open it and get it started. Otherwise..find a hydrolic jack and just roll the thing to another spot. You may need some help with that one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroFanaticus2||12-25-2001||12:54 AM||||I heard something about having GM replace the keys.  Anybody heard of this?  Who would I contact to have this done??  I've looked for hours for the keys but can't find them.  I need a metal detector!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smoooooth GT||12-25-2001||01:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroFanaticus2:<BR><B>I heard something about having GM replace the keys.  Anybody heard of this?  Who would I contact to have this done??  I've looked for hours for the keys but can't find them.  I need a metal detector!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, It sound's like you're having a Merry Christmas so far...  Just call a Locksmith and get back to having fun before you miss Christmas altogether!!!  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BABIE_BUN_SHAKERS.gif">                       <BR>      <P><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hank is Here||12-25-2001||10:24 AM||||Well just to buy you time.  find out whose space you are parked in give them a call and tell them to park in your space.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroFanaticus2||12-25-2001||03:36 PM||||Keys Found.  Problem solved.<BR>Had a car lined up in ohio I was going to go buy this weekend too.  Had my bags packed and was heading out to buy a greyhound ticket when my girlfriend looked down and just picked up the keys.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||ray b||12-26-2001||07:01 PM||||G M has key # for most of its cars<BR>and most dealers and locksmiths have masterskeys for most G M cars.<BR>you should all ways make spares but<BR>know your  Key # and a BIG locksmith BILL can be avoided any G M dealer can sell you a key if you know the #<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||12-26-2001||07:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>G M has key # for most of its cars<BR>and most dealers and locksmiths have masterskeys for most G M cars.<BR>you should all ways make spares but<BR>know your  Key # and a BIG locksmith BILL can be avoided any G M dealer can sell you a key if you know the #<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, that <B>is</B> a very good idea. Just write down the number on your key (usually 3 or 4 digits) and keep that in your wallet or something, so when you need a key quick (and still haven't gotten around to getting a spare) you can have one made in no time.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||12-26-2001||09:21 PM||||Now that you've found the keys, Just go to GM and have another set made. They usually will do 1 set for free. Then write down the code # they ket the keys to. (Some keys don't have the number code on them but the key machine at a GM dealer can tell you what it is.)<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
